// Title: Tomcat WebServer Logs Deleted
// Sigma ID: 270185ff-5f50-4d6d-a27f-24c3b8c9fef8
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-02-16 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1070
// Description: Detects the deletion of tomcat WebServer logs which may indicate an attempt to destroy forensic
//   evidence
// False positives:
//   - During uninstallation of the tomcat server
//   - During log rotation
// References:
//   - Internal Research
//   - https://linuxhint.com/view-tomcat-logs-windows/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/file/file_delete/file_delete_win_delete_tomcat_logs.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where ActionType =~ "FileDeleted" and ((FolderPath contains "\\Tomcat" and FolderPath contains "\\logs\\") and (FolderPath contains "catalina." or FolderPath contains "_access_log." or FolderPath contains "localhost."))
